window.LAB = [{"id":"ecs","title":"ECS on AWS","icon":"🐳","summary":"Dockerise the Memos example app, build its AWS platform with Terraform (VPC, ALB, ECS Fargate) and automate it with GitHub Actions.","stages":[{"title":"Set up your tools","icon":"🧰","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Every DevOps project starts the same way: the right tools on your machine and a <strong>safe</strong> AWS account. In this lab you'll take <strong>Memos</strong>, an open-source note-taking app, as your example project and build a production platform for it from nothing: <strong>Dockerise</strong> it, provision AWS with <strong>Terraform</strong>, and automate every change with a <strong>CI/CD pipeline</strong>. That's the same path a real team would take.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 <strong>Placeholders:</strong> wherever you see <code>your-username</code>, <code>example.com</code>, <code>memos-tfstate-example</code> or the account <code>123456789012</code>, use your own GitHub username, domain, bucket name and account.</p>\n<p>🔧 <strong>How the lab works:</strong> each step explains <strong>what</strong> and <strong>why</strong>, then gives you a command to type into the practice terminal. You can tap <strong>Run it for me</strong> on your phone. To do it for real, copy the commands into your own terminal.</p>\n</blockquote>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  L[\"💻 laptop<br/>git · docker · aws · terraform\"] --> GH[GitHub repo]\n  GH --> AWS[\"☁️ AWS: VPC · ALB · ECS · ECR\"]\n  AWS --> W[\"🌐 memos.example.com\"]","caption":"Where we're heading"}],"steps":[{"title":"Install Git and check it","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Git tracks every change to your code. On macOS run <code>brew install git</code>; on Ubuntu <code>sudo apt install -y git</code>.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git --version","output":"git version 2.47.1"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Tell Git who you are, once per machine:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git config --global user.name \"Your Name\"","output":"(no output means it worked)"}]},{"title":"Install Docker","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Docker builds and runs containers. Install <strong>Docker Desktop</strong> (Mac/Windows) or Docker Engine (Linux), then check:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker run --rm hello-world","output":"Unable to find image 'hello-world:latest' locally\nlatest: Pulling from library/hello-world\nStatus: Downloaded newer image for hello-world:latest\n\nHello from Docker!\nThis message shows that your installation appears to be working correctly."},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What did <code>docker run --rm hello-world</code> just do?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Built an image from a Dockerfile","ok":false},{"t":"Pulled an image from Docker Hub, ran it as a container, then removed the container (<code>--rm</code>)","ok":true},{"t":"Installed Docker","ok":false},{"t":"Pushed an image to ECR","ok":false}],"explain":"<p><code>run</code> = pull if missing → create → start. <code>--rm</code> cleans up the container when it exits.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Install the AWS CLI and Terraform","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The <strong>AWS CLI</strong> talks to AWS's APIs from your terminal. <strong>Terraform</strong> turns <code>.tf</code> files into real infrastructure. On macOS: <code>brew install awscli hashicorp/tap/terraform</code>.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws --version","output":"aws-cli/2.22.4 Python/3.12.6 Darwin/24.1.0 source/arm64"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform -version","output":"Terraform v1.13.5\non darwin_arm64"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ Match the pipeline's version (Memos pins <strong>1.13.5</strong>), so local and CI behave the same.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Secure the AWS account","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>In the AWS console, as root, do these <strong>once</strong>:\n1. Turn on <strong>MFA</strong> for the root user.\n2. <strong>Billing → Budgets →</strong> create a monthly budget (e.g. $20) with email alerts.\n3. Enable <strong>IAM Identity Center</strong> and create an admin user for yourself.\n4. Sign out of root and never use it day to day.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  ROOT[\"root user<br/>🔒 MFA · no keys · locked away\"] -.only for billing/emergencies.-> ACC[(AWS account)]\n  YOU[\"you via IAM Identity Center<br/>short-lived credentials\"] --> ACC"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why create a separate admin identity instead of using the root user?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Root can't use the CLI","ok":false},{"t":"Root has unlimited, unrestrictable power, so if it's compromised you lose the account; day-to-day work should use a separate, revocable identity","ok":true},{"t":"Identity Center is required for Terraform","ok":false},{"t":"It's cheaper","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Least privilege starts with you. Keep root locked away behind MFA.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Log in from the terminal","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Use <strong>SSO</strong> so your laptop gets short-lived credentials, not access keys stored in a file.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws configure sso","output":"SSO session name: memos\nSSO start URL: https://d-1234567890.awsapps.com/start\nSSO region: eu-west-1\nAttempting to automatically open the SSO authorization page in your default browser.\nSuccessfully logged into Start URL: https://d-1234567890.awsapps.com/start\nCLI default client Region [None]: eu-west-1\nProfile name: memos"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Then check who you are:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws sts get-caller-identity --profile memos","output":"{\n    \"UserId\": \"AROA3XFRBF23EXAMPLE:you\",\n    \"Account\": \"123456789012\",\n    \"Arn\": \"arn:aws:sts::123456789012:assumed-role/AWSReservedSSO_AdministratorAccess_ab12/you\"\n}"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 Run <code>export AWS_PROFILE=memos</code> so every later command uses this login.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]}]},{"title":"Create the repo and get the app","icon":"📁","time":"15 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Your infrastructure lives in its own repository (call it <strong>memos-aws-infra</strong>), with the Memos source code copied into an <code>app/</code> folder.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  R[memos-aws-infra/] --> A[\"app/ (Memos source)\"]\n  R --> D[Dockerfile]\n  R --> B[\"bootstrap/ (state + OIDC)\"]\n  R --> I[\"infra/ (main stack + modules)\"]\n  R --> W[\".github/workflows/\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Create the repository","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"mkdir memos-aws-infra && cd memos-aws-infra && git init","output":"Initialized empty Git repository in /Users/you/memos-aws-infra/.git/"}]},{"title":"Bring in the Memos source","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Copy the open-source app into <code>app/</code>. A shallow clone is enough, and you remove its <code>.git</code> so it becomes plain files in your repo.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/usememos/memos.git app && rm -rf app/.git","output":"Cloning into 'app'...\nremote: Enumerating objects: 1520, done.\nReceiving objects: 100% (1520/1520), 3.21 MiB | 9.80 MiB/s, done."}]},{"title":"Write a .gitignore (carefully)","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Keep build output, secrets and Terraform's local files out of Git.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"gitignore","code":".terraform/\n*.tfstate\n*.tfstate.*\n*.tfplan\n.env\n/memos","file":".gitignore"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 <strong>A classic bug:</strong> a first version often says <code>memos</code> (no slash). That also matched <code>app/cmd/memos/</code>, so <code>main.go</code> is never committed and CI fails. <strong><code>/memos</code></strong> only matches at the repo root.</p>\n</blockquote>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why does <code>/memos</code> in .gitignore behave differently from <code>memos</code>?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"It doesn't: they're identical","ok":false},{"t":"A leading <code>/</code> anchors the pattern to the repo root, so it only ignores a top-level <code>memos</code>, not every file or folder named memos","ok":true},{"t":"<code>/memos</code> ignores folders only","ok":false},{"t":"<code>/memos</code> is invalid syntax","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Unanchored patterns match at <strong>any depth</strong>. That's how <code>cmd/memos/</code> disappeared.</p>"}}]},{"title":"First commit and push","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Create an empty repo on GitHub under your own account called <strong>memos-aws-infra</strong>, then:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git add . && git commit -m \"Add Memos source\" && git push -u origin main","output":"[main (root-commit) 1a2b3c4] Add Memos source\n 1203 files changed, 98211 insertions(+)\nTo github.com:your-username/memos-aws-infra.git\n * [new branch]      main -> main"}]}]},{"title":"Containerise Memos","icon":"🐳","time":"40 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>You'll package Memos into a small, secure image with a <strong>three-stage</strong> Dockerfile, then run it locally.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  F[\"① frontend<br/>node:22-alpine\"] -->|dist/| B[\"② backend<br/>golang:1.25-alpine<br/>static binary\"]\n  B -->|/memos| R[\"③ runtime<br/>alpine:3.21 · user 1001 · :8081\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Stage 1: build the frontend","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The React frontend compiles into static files. Copy the <strong>lock files first</strong> so dependency installs are cached between builds.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"dockerfile","code":"FROM node:22-alpine AS frontend\nWORKDIR /build/web\nRUN npm install --global pnpm@10.24.0\nCOPY app/web/package.json app/web/pnpm-lock.yaml ./\nRUN pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\nCOPY app/web/ ./\nRUN pnpm release","file":"Dockerfile"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why copy <code>package.json</code> and the lock file <strong>before</strong> the rest of the frontend source?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"npm requires it","ok":false},{"t":"So the slow <code>pnpm install</code> layer is cached and only re-runs when dependencies change, not on every code edit","ok":true},{"t":"To make the image smaller","ok":false},{"t":"So the files are owned by root","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Order layers from least- to most-frequently changing.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Stage 2: compile the Go backend","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p><code>CGO_ENABLED=0</code> makes a <strong>static</strong> binary with no C libraries needed. <code>-ldflags=\"-s -w\"</code> strips debug info.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"dockerfile","code":"FROM golang:1.25-alpine AS backend\nWORKDIR /build\nRUN apk add --no-cache git ca-certificates\nCOPY app/go.mod app/go.sum ./\nRUN go mod download\nCOPY app/ ./\nCOPY --from=frontend /build/server/router/frontend/dist ./server/router/frontend/dist\nRUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags=\"-s -w\" -tags netgo,osusergo -o /memos ./cmd/memos","file":"Dockerfile"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 <strong>Common pitfall:</strong> if the builder image (say <code>golang:1.23</code>) is older than the Go version in <code>go.mod</code>, the build fails. Always match toolchain versions: here, <strong>1.25</strong>.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Stage 3: a tiny, non-root runtime","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Only the binary, CA certificates and time-zone data. A dedicated user, <strong>1001</strong>, owns the data folder.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"dockerfile","code":"FROM alpine:3.21 AS runtime\nRUN apk add --no-cache ca-certificates tzdata && \\\n    addgroup -S -g 1001 appuser && \\\n    adduser -S -D -u 1001 -G appuser appuser && \\\n    mkdir -p /var/opt/memos && chown appuser:appuser /var/opt/memos\nCOPY --from=backend /memos /usr/local/bin/memos\nWORKDIR /var/opt/memos\nENV MEMOS_PORT=8081 MEMOS_DATA=/var/opt/memos\nUSER 1001:1001\nEXPOSE 8081\nENTRYPOINT [\"memos\"]","file":"Dockerfile"}]},{"title":"Build the image","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p><code>--platform linux/amd64</code> matches Fargate's default CPU architecture, even if you're on an ARM Mac.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t memos:dev .","output":"[+] Building 212.4s (24/24) FINISHED\n => [frontend 5/6] RUN pnpm install --frozen-lockfile           58.1s\n => [backend 7/7] RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath ...      96.3s\n => [runtime 3/3] COPY --from=backend /memos /usr/local/bin/memos 0.1s\n => naming to docker.io/library/memos:dev"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker images memos","output":"REPOSITORY   TAG       IMAGE ID       CREATED          SIZE\nmemos        dev       4f1c9a2b7e3d   10 seconds ago   75.8MB"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 A single-stage build of the same code was <strong>2.79 GB</strong>. That's about 97% smaller.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Run it and test it","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Publish container port 8081 on your laptop and give it a volume so the data survives restarts.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker run -d --name memos -p 8081:8081 -v memos-data:/var/opt/memos memos:dev","output":"9b3e0c1d77f2a8c4e1f6a3b5d9e8c7f0a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6"},{"type":"term","cmd":"curl -i http://localhost:8081/healthz","output":"HTTP/1.1 200 OK\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n\nService ready."},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Open <strong>http://localhost:8081</strong> in a browser and you'll see Memos running locally.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Which user is the Memos process running as inside the container?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"root","ok":false},{"t":"UID 1001 (appuser)","ok":true},{"t":"nobody","ok":false},{"t":"the same user as your laptop","ok":false}],"explain":"<p><code>USER 1001:1001</code> in the Dockerfile. If the app were compromised, the attacker wouldn't be root.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Commit the Dockerfile","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"git add Dockerfile .dockerignore && git commit -m \"Add multi-stage Dockerfile\" && git push","output":"[main 5d6e7f8] Add multi-stage Dockerfile\n 2 files changed, 41 insertions(+)"}]}]},{"title":"Bootstrap: state bucket and OIDC","icon":"🪣","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Before the main infrastructure, you need two <strong>long-lived</strong> things: a place to store Terraform state, and a keyless identity for GitHub Actions. They live in their own <code>bootstrap/</code> stack.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  subgraph BOOT[\"bootstrap/ · local state · run once\"]\n    S3[(\"S3: memos-tfstate-example<br/>versioned · encrypted · private\")]\n    OIDC[\"IAM OIDC provider<br/>token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"]\n    ROLE[\"IAM role github-actions-role\"]\n  end\n  GHA[GitHub Actions] -->|\"AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"| ROLE"}],"steps":[{"title":"Provider configuration","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"terraform {\n  required_version = \">= 1.10.0, < 2.0.0\"\n  required_providers {\n    aws = { source = \"hashicorp/aws\", version = \"~> 5.0\" }\n  }\n}\n\nprovider \"aws\" {\n  region = \"eu-west-1\"\n  default_tags {\n    tags = { Project = \"Memos\", ManagedBy = \"Terraform\" }\n  }\n}","file":"bootstrap/provider.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p><code>default_tags</code> stamps every resource, which makes cost reports and clean-up easy.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"The state bucket","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"state\" {\n  bucket = \"memos-tfstate-example\"   # globally unique: use your own\n  lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }\n}\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_versioning\" \"state\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.state.id\n  versioning_configuration { status = \"Enabled\" }\n}\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration\" \"state\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.state.id\n  rule {\n    apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {\n      sse_algorithm = \"AES256\"\n    }\n  }\n}\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block\" \"state\" {\n  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.state.id\n  block_public_acls       = true\n  block_public_policy     = true\n  ignore_public_acls      = true\n  restrict_public_buckets = true\n}","file":"bootstrap/state.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Plus a bucket policy that <strong>denies any request not using HTTPS</strong> (<code>aws:SecureTransport = false</code>).</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What does <code>prevent_destroy = true</code> protect against?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Someone deleting objects in the bucket","ok":false},{"t":"Terraform destroying the bucket, even when running <code>terraform destroy</code>","ok":true},{"t":"Public access to the bucket","ok":false},{"t":"Encryption being turned off","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>It's a Terraform safety catch. Versioning protects the <strong>objects</strong> inside.</p>"}}]},{"title":"The OIDC provider and role","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>GitHub signs a token for each workflow run. AWS trusts that token <strong>only</strong> for your repo.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_iam_openid_connect_provider\" \"github\" {\n  url            = \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n  client_id_list = [\"sts.amazonaws.com\"]\n  thumbprint_list = [\"ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff\"]\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"github_actions\" {\n  name = \"github-actions-role\"\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n      Principal = { Federated = aws_iam_openid_connect_provider.github.arn }\n      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n      Condition = {\n        StringEquals = { \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\" }\n        StringLike   = { \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub\" = \"repo:your-username/memos-aws-infra:*\" }\n      }\n    }]\n  })\n}","file":"bootstrap/oidc.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ To keep the first version simple, attach <strong>AdministratorAccess</strong> to this role. It works, but it's too broad, and in stage 15 you'll tighten it.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Apply the bootstrap","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"cd bootstrap && terraform init","output":"Initializing provider plugins...\n- Installing hashicorp/aws v5.82.2...\nTerraform has been successfully initialized!"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply","output":"Plan: 8 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.\n\nDo you want to perform these actions?\n  Enter a value: yes\n\naws_s3_bucket.state: Creation complete after 2s [id=memos-tfstate-example]\naws_iam_openid_connect_provider.github: Creation complete after 1s\naws_iam_role.github_actions: Creation complete after 1s [id=github-actions-role]\n\nApply complete! Resources: 8 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."}]},{"title":"Give GitHub the role ARN","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>In GitHub: <strong>Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New secret</strong> named <code>AWS_ROLE_ARN</code>, with the role's ARN as the value.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws iam get-role --role-name github-actions-role --query Role.Arn --output text","output":"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/github-actions-role"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Is the role ARN a sensitive credential?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Yes, it's as dangerous as an access key","ok":false},{"t":"Not really: it's an identifier; only workflows matching the trust policy can assume it. It's stored as a secret mainly for tidiness","ok":true},{"t":"Yes, anyone with it can log in to AWS","ok":false},{"t":"It expires after an hour","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>The protection is the <strong>trust policy</strong> (<code>aud</code> + <code>sub</code>), not the secrecy of the ARN.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Terraform skeleton for the main stack","icon":"🏗️","time":"20 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Now the main stack in <code>infra/</code>. Its state lives in the bucket you just created.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  P[provider.tf<br/>backend s3 + lockfile] --> M[main.tf<br/>calls 7 modules]\n  V[variables.tf] --> M\n  T[terraform.tfvars<br/>real values] --> V\n  M --> O[outputs.tf]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Backend and provider","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"terraform {\n  required_version = \">= 1.10.0, < 2.0.0\"\n  required_providers {\n    aws = { source = \"hashicorp/aws\", version = \"~> 5.0\" }\n  }\n  backend \"s3\" {\n    bucket       = \"memos-tfstate-example\"\n    key          = \"prod/terraform.tfstate\"\n    region       = \"eu-west-1\"\n    encrypt      = true\n    use_lockfile = true      # S3 native locking (Terraform 1.10+)\n  }\n}\n\nprovider \"aws\" {\n  region = var.aws_region\n  default_tags { tags = { Project = \"Memos\", ManagedBy = \"Terraform\" } }\n}","file":"infra/provider.tf"}]},{"title":"Variables and values","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Declare inputs in <code>variables.tf</code>, and put the real values in <code>terraform.tfvars</code>:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"project_name = \"memos\"\nenvironment  = \"prod\"\naws_region   = \"eu-west-1\"\ndomain_name  = \"example.com\"\n\nvpc_cidr             = \"10.0.0.0/16\"\npublic_subnet_cidrs  = [\"10.0.1.0/24\", \"10.0.2.0/24\"]\nprivate_subnet_cidrs = [\"10.0.3.0/24\", \"10.0.4.0/24\"]\navailability_zones   = [\"eu-west-1a\", \"eu-west-1b\"]\n\nrepository_name = \"memos\"","file":"infra/terraform.tfvars"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p><code>image_url</code> has a default of <code>\"\"</code> and is passed in by the pipeline with each deploy.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Initialise with the remote backend","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"cd ../infra && terraform init","output":"Initializing the backend...\nSuccessfully configured the backend \"s3\"! Terraform will automatically\nuse this backend unless the backend configuration changes.\nInitializing modules...\nTerraform has been successfully initialized!"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Where will this stack's state be stored?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"In <code>infra/terraform.tfstate</code> on your laptop","ok":false},{"t":"In S3 at <code>memos-tfstate-example/prod/terraform.tfstate</code>, locked with a <code>.tflock</code> object","ok":true},{"t":"In GitHub","ok":false},{"t":"In DynamoDB","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Shared by you and CI, versioned, encrypted, and locked during applies.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Build the network","icon":"🏘️","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>A VPC across two AZs, with public subnets for the load balancer and NAT, and private subnets for the app.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  I((Internet)) <--> IGW[Internet gateway]\n  subgraph VPC[\"VPC 10.0.0.0/16\"]\n    subgraph A[\"eu-west-1a\"]\n      PA[\"public 10.0.1.0/24<br/>NAT-a\"] \n      RA[\"private 10.0.3.0/24\"]\n    end\n    subgraph B[\"eu-west-1b\"]\n      PB[\"public 10.0.2.0/24<br/>NAT-b\"]\n      RB[\"private 10.0.4.0/24\"]\n    end\n  end\n  IGW <--> PA & PB\n  RA -->|0.0.0.0/0| PA\n  RB -->|0.0.0.0/0| PB"}],"steps":[{"title":"VPC and subnets","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_vpc\" \"main\" {\n  cidr_block           = var.vpc_cidr\n  enable_dns_hostnames = true\n  enable_dns_support   = true\n}\n\nresource \"aws_subnet\" \"public\" {\n  count             = length(var.public_subnet_cidrs)\n  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id\n  cidr_block        = var.public_subnet_cidrs[count.index]\n  availability_zone = data.aws_availability_zones.available.names[count.index]\n}\n\nresource \"aws_subnet\" \"private\" {\n  count             = length(var.private_subnet_cidrs)\n  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id\n  cidr_block        = var.private_subnet_cidrs[count.index]\n  availability_zone = data.aws_availability_zones.available.names[count.index]\n}","file":"infra/modules/vpc/main.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p><code>count</code> creates one subnet per CIDR in the list, and each lands in a different AZ.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Internet gateway and NAT gateways","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>One NAT gateway <strong>per AZ</strong>, each with its own Elastic IP, so one AZ failing doesn't cut off the other's outbound traffic.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_internet_gateway\" \"main\" { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id }\n\nresource \"aws_eip\" \"nat\" {\n  count  = length(var.public_subnet_cidrs)\n  domain = \"vpc\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_nat_gateway\" \"main\" {\n  count         = length(var.public_subnet_cidrs)\n  allocation_id = aws_eip.nat[count.index].id\n  subnet_id     = aws_subnet.public[count.index].id\n  depends_on    = [aws_internet_gateway.main]\n}","file":"infra/modules/vpc/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Route tables","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The public route table sends internet traffic to the <strong>IGW</strong>. Each private route table sends it to <strong>its own AZ's NAT</strong>.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_route_table\" \"public\" {\n  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id\n  route {\n    cidr_block = \"0.0.0.0/0\"\n    gateway_id = aws_internet_gateway.main.id\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_route_table\" \"private\" {\n  count  = length(var.private_subnet_cidrs)\n  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id\n  route {\n    cidr_block     = \"0.0.0.0/0\"\n    nat_gateway_id = aws_nat_gateway.main[count.index].id\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/vpc/main.tf"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What makes <code>10.0.1.0/24</code> a <strong>public</strong> subnet?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Its CIDR range","ok":false},{"t":"It's in AZ a","ok":false},{"t":"Its route table sends <code>0.0.0.0/0</code> to the internet gateway","ok":true},{"t":"It has a NAT gateway","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>\"Public\" is defined by the <strong>route</strong>, not a setting.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Call the module and apply","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"module \"vpc\" {\n  source               = \"./modules/vpc\"\n  project_name         = var.project_name\n  environment          = var.environment\n  vpc_cidr             = var.vpc_cidr\n  public_subnet_cidrs  = var.public_subnet_cidrs\n  private_subnet_cidrs = var.private_subnet_cidrs\n  availability_zones   = var.availability_zones\n}","file":"infra/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -target=module.vpc","output":"Plan: 15 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.\nmodule.vpc.aws_vpc.main: Creation complete after 2s [id=vpc-0a1b2c3d4e5f67890]\nmodule.vpc.aws_nat_gateway.main[0]: Still creating... [1m30s elapsed]\nmodule.vpc.aws_nat_gateway.main[1]: Creation complete after 1m44s\nApply complete! Resources: 15 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ <code>-target</code> is handy while learning, building one piece at a time. Day to day, run plain <code>plan</code>/<code>apply</code> so the whole stack stays consistent. NAT gateways now cost money every hour, so <code>terraform destroy</code> at the end of a session if you're practising.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]}]},{"title":"Security groups","icon":"🔒","time":"15 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Two firewalls: one for the ALB (open to the world on 80/443) and one for the tasks (open <strong>only</strong> to the ALB, on 8081).</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  W((Internet)) -->|80, 443| ALB[ALB SG]\n  ALB -->|8081| ECS[ECS SG]\n  ECS -->|443| OUT((\"ECR, S3, Logs<br/>via NAT\"))"}],"steps":[{"title":"Two empty groups","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_security_group\" \"alb\" {\n  name   = \"${var.project_name}-${var.environment}-alb-sg\"\n  vpc_id = var.vpc_id\n}\nresource \"aws_security_group\" \"ecs\" {\n  name   = \"${var.project_name}-${var.environment}-ecs-sg\"\n  vpc_id = var.vpc_id\n}","file":"infra/modules/security/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Rules as separate resources","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Separate rule resources are easier to read and change than inline blocks. Note the <strong>SG-to-SG</strong> references:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule\" \"alb_https\" {\n  security_group_id = aws_security_group.alb.id\n  cidr_ipv4         = \"0.0.0.0/0\"\n  ip_protocol       = \"tcp\"\n  from_port         = 443\n  to_port           = 443\n}\nresource \"aws_vpc_security_group_egress_rule\" \"alb_to_ecs\" {\n  security_group_id            = aws_security_group.alb.id\n  referenced_security_group_id = aws_security_group.ecs.id\n  ip_protocol = \"tcp\"\n  from_port   = 8081\n  to_port     = 8081\n}\nresource \"aws_vpc_security_group_ingress_rule\" \"ecs_from_alb\" {\n  security_group_id            = aws_security_group.ecs.id\n  referenced_security_group_id = aws_security_group.alb.id\n  ip_protocol = \"tcp\"\n  from_port   = 8081\n  to_port     = 8081\n}\nresource \"aws_vpc_security_group_egress_rule\" \"ecs_https\" {\n  security_group_id = aws_security_group.ecs.id\n  cidr_ipv4         = \"0.0.0.0/0\"\n  ip_protocol       = \"tcp\"\n  from_port         = 443\n  to_port           = 443\n}","file":"infra/modules/security/main.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>There's also a port-80 ingress rule on the ALB, used only for the HTTPS redirect.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What would break if you deleted the <code>alb_to_ecs</code> <strong>egress</strong> rule?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Nothing: security groups are stateful","ok":false},{"t":"The ALB couldn't open connections to the tasks on 8081, so health checks fail and users get errors","ok":true},{"t":"Only HTTPS would break","ok":false},{"t":"The NAT gateway would stop","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Stateful means <strong>replies</strong> are allowed automatically. The ALB still needs an egress rule to <strong>start</strong> connections to the targets.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"ECR and your first image push","icon":"📦","time":"20 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Create the private registry, then push the image you built in stage 3.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  L[\"💻 memos:dev\"] -->|docker tag| T[\"…/memos:3f9c2e1…\"] -->|docker push| ECR[(\"ECR memos<br/>IMMUTABLE · scan on push\")]"}],"steps":[{"title":"The repository","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecr_repository\" \"this\" {\n  name                 = var.repository_name\n  image_tag_mutability = \"IMMUTABLE\"\n  force_delete         = true\n  image_scanning_configuration { scan_on_push = true }\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecr/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -target=module.ecr","output":"module.ecr.aws_ecr_repository.this: Creation complete after 1s [id=memos]\nApply complete! Resources: 1 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."}]},{"title":"Log Docker in to ECR","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"aws ecr get-login-password | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com","output":"Login Succeeded"}]},{"title":"Tag with the commit SHA and push","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"docker tag memos:dev 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/memos:$(git rev-parse HEAD)","output":"(no output means it worked)"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker push 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/memos:$(git rev-parse HEAD)","output":"The push refers to repository [123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/memos]\n5f70bf18a086: Pushed\n3f9c2e1d…: digest: sha256:9a8b7c… size: 1157"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>You run the same <code>docker push</code> again. What happens?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"It overwrites the old image","ok":false},{"t":"ECR rejects it: the tag already exists and tags are immutable","ok":true},{"t":"It creates <code>memos:sha-2</code>","ok":false},{"t":"It deletes the old image first","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>That's the \"re-run\" problem <code>build.yml</code> solves by checking ECR first and reusing the image.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"DNS and the certificate","icon":"🔐","time":"20 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Look up your Route 53 hosted zone, then request an ACM certificate that Terraform validates automatically.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"sequenceDiagram\n  participant TF as Terraform\n  participant ACM\n  participant R53 as Route 53\n  TF->>ACM: request cert (example.com + memos.example.com)\n  ACM-->>TF: validation CNAMEs\n  TF->>R53: create the CNAMEs\n  ACM->>R53: check\n  ACM-->>TF: ISSUED ✅"}],"steps":[{"title":"Find the hosted zone","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The domain is already registered and its hosted zone exists, so Terraform just <strong>looks it up</strong> with a data source:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"data \"aws_route53_zone\" \"main\" {\n  name         = var.domain_name\n  private_zone = false\n}","file":"infra/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws route53 list-hosted-zones-by-name --dns-name example.com --query \"HostedZones[0].Id\"","output":"\"/hostedzone/Z0123456789ABCDEFGHIJ\""}]},{"title":"Request and validate the certificate","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_acm_certificate\" \"this\" {\n  domain_name               = var.domain_name\n  subject_alternative_names = [\"memos.${var.domain_name}\"]\n  validation_method         = \"DNS\"\n  lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_route53_record\" \"validation\" {\n  for_each = {\n    for o in aws_acm_certificate.this.domain_validation_options : o.domain_name => {\n      name = o.resource_record_name, type = o.resource_record_type, record = o.resource_record_value\n    }\n  }\n  zone_id = var.zone_id\n  name    = each.value.name\n  type    = each.value.type\n  records = [each.value.record]\n  ttl     = 60\n}\n\nresource \"aws_acm_certificate_validation\" \"this\" {\n  certificate_arn         = aws_acm_certificate.this.arn\n  validation_record_fqdns = [for r in aws_route53_record.validation : r.fqdn]\n}","file":"infra/modules/acm/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -target=module.acm","output":"module.acm.aws_acm_certificate.this: Creation complete after 9s\nmodule.acm.aws_route53_record.validation[\"example.com\"]: Creation complete after 35s\nmodule.acm.aws_route53_record.validation[\"memos.example.com\"]: Creation complete after 35s\nmodule.acm.aws_acm_certificate_validation.this: Still creating... [1m0s elapsed]\nmodule.acm.aws_acm_certificate_validation.this: Creation complete after 1m12s"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why <code>for_each</code> here rather than <code>count</code>?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"count doesn't work with Route 53","ok":false},{"t":"The validation options are keyed by domain name, so for_each gives stable keys that don't shift if a domain is added or removed","ok":true},{"t":"for_each is required by ACM","ok":false},{"t":"count would create duplicate certificates","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Stable keys mean stable resources.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"The load balancer","icon":"⚖️","time":"25 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The public front door: port 80 redirects, port 443 terminates TLS and forwards to the tasks on 8081.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  U((users)) --> L80[\":80\"] -->|301| L443[\":443 · ACM\"]\n  U --> L443 --> TG[\"target group · ip · 8081<br/>health check /\"] --> T[\"tasks\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"ALB and target group","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_lb\" \"this\" {\n  name                       = \"${var.project_name}-alb\"\n  internal                   = false\n  load_balancer_type         = \"application\"\n  drop_invalid_header_fields = true\n  security_groups            = [var.security_group]\n  subnets                    = var.public_subnets\n}\n\nresource \"aws_lb_target_group\" \"this\" {\n  name        = \"${var.project_name}-tg\"\n  port        = 8081\n  protocol    = \"HTTP\"\n  vpc_id      = var.vpc_id\n  target_type = \"ip\"            # Fargate tasks register by IP\n  health_check {\n    path                = \"/\"\n    matcher             = \"200-399\"\n    interval            = 30\n    healthy_threshold   = 2\n    unhealthy_threshold = 2\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/alb/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Listeners: redirect and forward","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_lb_listener\" \"http\" {\n  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.this.arn\n  port              = 80\n  protocol          = \"HTTP\"\n  default_action {\n    type = \"redirect\"\n    redirect {\n      port        = \"443\"\n      protocol    = \"HTTPS\"\n      status_code = \"HTTP_301\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_lb_listener\" \"https\" {\n  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.this.arn\n  port              = 443\n  protocol          = \"HTTPS\"\n  ssl_policy        = \"ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06\"\n  certificate_arn   = var.certificate_arn\n  default_action {\n    type             = \"forward\"\n    target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.this.arn\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/alb/main.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -target=module.alb","output":"module.alb.aws_lb.this: Still creating... [2m0s elapsed]\nmodule.alb.aws_lb.this: Creation complete after 2m31s\nApply complete! Resources: 4 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why does the target group use <code>target_type = \"ip\"</code> for Fargate?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"The ALB only supports IP targets","ok":false},{"t":"Fargate has no EC2 instance to register; each task gets its own network interface and private IP (awsvpc mode), so targets are task IPs","ok":true},{"t":"IP targets are cheaper","ok":false},{"t":"It's needed for HTTPS","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>ALBs support instance, IP and Lambda targets. Fargate tasks are reached by their own IPs.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"IAM roles for ECS","icon":"🎭","time":"10 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Two roles with two different jobs.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  ECS[\"ECS agent\"] -->|assumes| ER[\"execution role<br/>pull ECR · write logs\"]\n  APP[\"Memos code\"] -->|assumes| TR[\"task role<br/>(no permissions)\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Trust ECS, then attach permissions","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"data \"aws_iam_policy_document\" \"ecs_assume_role_policy\" {\n  statement {\n    actions = [\"sts:AssumeRole\"]\n    principals {\n      type        = \"Service\"\n      identifiers = [\"ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"execution_role\" {\n  name               = \"${var.project_name}-ecs-execution-role\"\n  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.ecs_assume_role_policy.json\n}\nresource \"aws_iam_role_policy_attachment\" \"execution_policy\" {\n  role       = aws_iam_role.execution_role.name\n  policy_arn = \"arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"task_role\" {\n  name               = \"${var.project_name}-ecs-task-role\"\n  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.ecs_assume_role_policy.json\n}","file":"infra/modules/iam/main.tf"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Memos never calls AWS APIs itself. Which role can therefore have <strong>no</strong> permissions attached?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"The execution role","ok":false},{"t":"The task role","ok":true},{"t":"Both","ok":false},{"t":"Neither","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>The execution role still needs ECR pull and CloudWatch Logs permissions so ECS can start the task.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Run Memos on ECS and go live","icon":"🚀","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The final piece: a cluster, a task definition, a service wired to the ALB, and a DNS record. After this, <strong>memos.example.com</strong> is live.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  U([User]) --> R53[Route 53 alias] --> ALB\n  subgraph VPC\n    ALB[ALB · public] -->|8081| T[Fargate task · private]\n  end\n  T --> ECR[(ECR)]\n  T --> CW[CloudWatch /ecs/memos]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Cluster and log group","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecs_cluster\" \"this\" {\n  name = \"${var.project_name}-cluster\"\n  setting {                       # cost trade-off\n    name  = \"containerInsights\"\n    value = \"disabled\"\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"aws_cloudwatch_log_group\" \"this\" {\n  name              = \"/ecs/${var.project_name}\"\n  retention_in_days = 7\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"}]},{"title":"The task definition","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecs_task_definition\" \"this\" {\n  family                   = \"${var.project_name}-task\"\n  requires_compatibilities = [\"FARGATE\"]\n  network_mode             = \"awsvpc\"\n  cpu                      = var.cpu          # 256 = 0.25 vCPU\n  memory                   = var.memory       # 512 MB\n  execution_role_arn       = var.execution_role_arn\n  task_role_arn            = var.task_role_arn\n  container_definitions = jsonencode([{\n    name         = \"memos\"\n    image        = var.image_url\n    essential    = true\n    portMappings = [{ containerPort = var.container_port, hostPort = var.container_port, protocol = \"tcp\" }]\n    logConfiguration = {\n      logDriver = \"awslogs\"\n      options = {\n        \"awslogs-group\"         = aws_cloudwatch_log_group.this.name\n        \"awslogs-region\"        = \"eu-west-1\"\n        \"awslogs-stream-prefix\" = \"ecs\"\n      }\n    }\n  }])\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"}]},{"title":"The service","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecs_service\" \"this\" {\n  name            = \"${var.project_name}-service\"\n  cluster         = aws_ecs_cluster.this.id\n  task_definition = aws_ecs_task_definition.this.arn\n  desired_count   = var.desired_count     # 1\n  launch_type     = \"FARGATE\"\n  network_configuration {\n    subnets          = var.private_subnet_ids\n    security_groups  = [var.ecs_security_group_id]\n    assign_public_ip = false\n  }\n  load_balancer {\n    target_group_arn = var.target_group_arn\n    container_name   = \"memos\"\n    container_port   = var.container_port\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Point the domain at the ALB","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_route53_record\" \"app\" {\n  zone_id = data.aws_route53_zone.main.zone_id\n  name    = \"memos.${var.domain_name}\"\n  type    = \"A\"\n  alias {\n    name                   = module.alb.dns_name\n    zone_id                = module.alb.alb_zone_id\n    evaluate_target_health = true\n  }\n}","file":"infra/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Apply everything","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Now run a full plan and apply with the image you pushed:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform apply -var=\"image_url=123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/memos:$(git rev-parse HEAD)\"","output":"Plan: 9 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.\nmodule.ecs.aws_ecs_cluster.this: Creation complete after 11s\nmodule.ecs.aws_ecs_task_definition.this: Creation complete after 1s [id=memos-task]\nmodule.ecs.aws_ecs_service.this: Creation complete after 2s\naws_route53_record.app: Creation complete after 41s [id=Z0123…_memos.example.com_A]\n\nOutputs:\napp_url = \"https://memos.example.com\""}]},{"title":"Watch the service become healthy","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"aws ecs describe-services --cluster memos-cluster --services memos-service --query \"services[0].events[0:3].message\"","output":"[\n    \"(service memos-service) has reached a steady state.\",\n    \"(service memos-service) registered 1 targets in (target-group memos-tg)\",\n    \"(service memos-service) has started 1 tasks: (task 7d1e…).\"\n]"},{"type":"term","cmd":"curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" https://memos.example.com/healthz","output":"200"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>🎉 <strong>Memos is live on AWS.</strong></p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>A user visits <code>http://memos.example.com</code>. Put the journey in order.</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"ECS → ALB → Route 53 → browser","ok":false},{"t":"Route 53 alias → ALB :80 → 301 to https → ALB :443 (TLS with ACM) → target group → task on 8081","ok":true},{"t":"NAT gateway → ECS → ALB","ok":false},{"t":"ACM → Route 53 → ECS","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Be able to say this in one breath. It's the most common \"explain your project\" question.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Automate it with GitHub Actions","icon":"🔁","time":"45 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Everything so far was by hand. Now a push to <code>main</code> will build, scan, push and deploy automatically, with no stored AWS keys.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  P[push to main] --> B[\"build.yml<br/>tfsec · OIDC · build or reuse image\"] --> D[\"deploy.yml<br/>fmt · validate · plan · apply\"] --> H[\"curl /healthz\"]\n  M[manual] --> X[\"destroy.yml\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"build.yml: triggers and permissions","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"name: Build and Push\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n    paths: ['app/**', 'Dockerfile', '.dockerignore']\n  workflow_dispatch:\nenv:\n  AWS_REGION: eu-west-1\n  ECR_REPOSITORY: memos\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      id-token: write     # allow OIDC\n      contents: read","file":".github/workflows/build.yml"}]},{"title":"build.yml: log in with OIDC","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - name: Scan Terraform security\n        uses: aquasecurity/tfsec-action@v1.0.3\n        with: { working_directory: infra }\n      - name: Configure AWS credentials\n        uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: ${{ secrets.AWS_ROLE_ARN }}\n          aws-region: ${{ env.AWS_REGION }}\n      - id: login-ecr\n        uses: aws-actions/amazon-ecr-login@v2","file":".github/workflows/build.yml"}]},{"title":"build.yml: build or reuse the image","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Idempotent: if the SHA's image already exists, reuse it. Only <code>ImageNotFoundException</code> triggers a build, and any other error fails loudly.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"      - name: Build or reuse image\n        env:\n          ECR_REGISTRY: ${{ steps.login-ecr.outputs.registry }}\n          IMAGE_TAG: ${{ github.sha }}\n        run: |\n          IMAGE=\"$ECR_REGISTRY/$ECR_REPOSITORY:$IMAGE_TAG\"\n          ERROR_FILE=$(mktemp)\n          if aws ecr describe-images --repository-name \"$ECR_REPOSITORY\" \\\n               --image-ids \"imageTag=$IMAGE_TAG\" > /dev/null 2>\"$ERROR_FILE\"; then\n            echo \"Image already exists; reusing $IMAGE\"\n          elif grep -q ImageNotFoundException \"$ERROR_FILE\"; then\n            docker build -t \"$IMAGE\" .\n            docker push \"$IMAGE\"\n          else\n            cat \"$ERROR_FILE\" >&2; exit 1\n          fi","file":".github/workflows/build.yml"}]},{"title":"deploy.yml: run after a successful build","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"name: Deploy\non:\n  workflow_run:\n    workflows: [\"Build and Push\"]\n    types: [completed]\n    branches: [main]\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      image_tag:\n        description: \"Full commit SHA of an existing ECR image\"\n        required: true\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    if: ${{ github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' || github.event.workflow_run.conclusion == 'success' }}","file":".github/workflows/deploy.yml"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>The deploy job checks the SHA is 40 characters and exists in ECR, then runs <code>terraform fmt -check</code>, <code>init</code>, <code>validate</code>, <code>plan -out=tfplan</code> and <code>apply tfplan</code> with <code>image_url</code> set.</p>"}]},{"title":"deploy.yml: verify it worked","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"  health-check:\n    needs: deploy\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: sleep 60\n      - run: |\n          code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" --max-time 30 https://memos.example.com/healthz)\n          if [ \"$code\" = \"200\" ]; then echo \"✅ Health check passed\"; else echo \"❌ got $code\"; exit 1; fi","file":".github/workflows/deploy.yml"}]},{"title":"Push and watch it run","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Make a small change in <code>app/</code> and push:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git commit -am \"Tweak app title\" && git push","output":"[main 3f9c2e1] Tweak app title\nTo github.com:your-username/memos-aws-infra.git\n   5d6e7f8..3f9c2e1  main -> main"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>In GitHub → <strong>Actions</strong>: <em>Build and Push</em> ✅ → <em>Deploy</em> ✅ → <em>Post Deploy Health Check</em> ✅.</p>"}]},{"title":"Practise a rollback","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>A bad version went out? <strong>Actions → Deploy → Run workflow</strong>, with <code>image_tag</code> set to the previous good SHA:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"gh workflow run deploy.yml -f image_tag=5d6e7f8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2c3d4e","output":"✓ Created workflow_dispatch event for deploy.yml at main"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why can you trust that this rollback deploys exactly the old code?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Terraform keeps old versions of the app","ok":false},{"t":"ECR tags are immutable, so that SHA tag can only ever point at the image built from that commit","ok":true},{"t":"GitHub caches old builds","ok":false},{"t":"ECS remembers old task definitions","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Immutable, SHA-tagged artefacts are what make rollbacks boring, and boring is good.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Break it and fix it","icon":"🧯","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The best way to learn troubleshooting is to cause real failures on purpose, then fix them. Try these on a practice environment, never on something real users depend on.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  S([symptom]) --> D{\"502 / 503 / 504?\"}\n  D -->|503| E[\"ECS: task running?<br/>stopped reason\"]\n  D -->|502| L[\"logs: app crashing?<br/>wrong port?\"]\n  D -->|504 / timeout| N[\"SGs · routes · NACLs\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Drill 1: port drift","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Change <code>MEMOS_PORT</code> to <code>5230</code> in the Dockerfile (Memos' default) but leave everything else on 8081. Deploy.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws elbv2 describe-target-health --target-group-arn arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:eu-west-1:123456789012:targetgroup/memos-tg/abc123 --query \"TargetHealthDescriptions[0].TargetHealth\"","output":"{\n    \"State\": \"unhealthy\",\n    \"Reason\": \"Target.FailedHealthChecks\",\n    \"Description\": \"Health checks failed\"\n}"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What's the fix that stops this ever happening again?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Open port 5230 in the security groups as well","ok":false},{"t":"Define the port once (a variable used by the image env, task definition, target group and SG rules) so they can't drift apart","ok":true},{"t":"Turn off health checks","ok":false},{"t":"Use port 80 everywhere","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Port drift (5230 vs 8081) is one of the most common reasons targets go unhealthy. Keep one source of truth for each value.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Drill 2: read the logs","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>When the task is crashing, the answer is usually in the logs:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws logs tail /ecs/memos --since 15m --follow","output":"2026-11-03T16:07:34 ecs/memos/7d1e… Memos 0.25.x started successfully!\n2026-11-03T16:07:34 ecs/memos/7d1e… Data directory: /var/opt/memos\n2026-11-03T16:07:34 ecs/memos/7d1e… Server running on port 8081"}]},{"title":"Drill 3: why did the task stop?","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"aws ecs describe-tasks --cluster memos-cluster --tasks 7d1e0c4b --query \"tasks[0].[stoppedReason,containers[0].exitCode]\"","output":"[\n    \"Essential container in task exited\",\n    137\n]"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Exit code 137 on this task most likely means…</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"the image wasn't found","ok":false},{"t":"the container was killed with SIGKILL, almost always for going over its 512 MB memory limit","ok":true},{"t":"a normal shutdown","ok":false},{"t":"a health check timeout","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>137 = 128 + 9. Raise the memory (a valid Fargate pair) and find out why usage grows.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Drill 4: drift","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Add an SSH rule to the ECS security group in the console, then:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"terraform plan -refresh-only","output":"Note: Objects have changed outside of Terraform\n  # module.security.aws_security_group.ecs has changed\nTerraform detected the following changes made outside of Terraform since the last apply."},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Remove the hand-made rule, and talk about <strong>why</strong> changes go through code.</p>"}]}]},{"title":"Level up: production improvements","icon":"🌟","time":"60 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The platform works. These upgrades turn it into something you'd defend in a senior interview. Each one matches a known limitation.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  A[RDS / EFS data tier] --> B[2+ tasks + autoscaling] --> C[circuit breaker + /healthz] --> D[least-privilege CI] --> E[plan on PR + approval]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Automatic rollback and a better health check","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecs_service\" \"this\" {\n  # …\n  health_check_grace_period_seconds = 60\n  deployment_circuit_breaker {\n    enable   = true\n    rollback = true\n  }\n}","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"health_check {\n  path    = \"/healthz\"     # the real liveness endpoint\n  matcher = \"200\"\n}","file":"infra/modules/alb/main.tf"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What does the circuit breaker add on top of the pipeline's <code>/healthz</code> check?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Faster image builds","ok":false},{"t":"ECS itself stops a failing rollout and returns to the last working deployment, with no human or pipeline needed","ok":true},{"t":"HTTPS","ok":false},{"t":"Auto scaling","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>The pipeline <strong>detects</strong> a bad deploy. The circuit breaker <strong>recovers</strong> from it.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Lock down the CI role","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Only <code>main</code> may assume the role, and with fewer permissions:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"StringLike = {\n  \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub\" = \"repo:your-username/memos-aws-infra:ref:refs/heads/main\"\n}","file":"bootstrap/oidc.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Then replace <code>AdministratorAccess</code> with a policy listing the ECR, ECS, ELB, EC2, IAM (scoped), ACM, Route 53, Logs and state-bucket actions Terraform actually uses. Pin third-party actions to commit SHAs while you're there.</p>"}]},{"title":"Move the data out of the container","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Memos supports Postgres. Add RDS in the private subnets and pass the DSN as a secret:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"container_definitions = jsonencode([{\n  name  = \"memos\"\n  image = var.image_url\n  environment = [{ name = \"MEMOS_DRIVER\", value = \"postgres\" }]\n  secrets     = [{ name = \"MEMOS_DSN\", valueFrom = var.dsn_secret_arn }]\n  # …\n}])","file":"infra/modules/ecs/main.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Give the <strong>execution role</strong> <code>secretsmanager:GetSecretValue</code> on that secret, allow 5432 from the ECS SG to an RDS SG, and then <code>desired_count = 2</code>.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>After moving to RDS, why is it now safe to run two tasks?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Fargate gives each task more memory","ok":false},{"t":"The tasks are stateless: both read and write the same database instead of their own local SQLite files","ok":true},{"t":"The ALB can now route to two targets","ok":false},{"t":"RDS makes tasks start faster","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Stateless app tier plus a shared, durable data tier: that's the pattern behind almost every scalable web app.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Plan on every pull request","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"on:\n  pull_request:\n    paths: ['infra/**']\njobs:\n  plan:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions: { id-token: write, contents: read, pull-requests: write }\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4\n        with: { role-to-assume: \"${{ secrets.AWS_PLAN_ROLE_ARN }}\", aws-region: eu-west-1 }\n      - uses: hashicorp/setup-terraform@v3\n      - run: terraform init && terraform plan -no-color | tee plan.txt\n        working-directory: infra","file":".github/workflows/plan.yml"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Post <code>plan.txt</code> as a PR comment, and require a reviewer on a protected <code>production</code> environment before <code>apply</code>. Reviewers see <strong>exactly</strong> what will change.</p>"}]}]}]},{"id":"eks","title":"EKS assignment","icon":"☸️","summary":"Complete the CoderCo EKS assignment: run the 2048 game on EKS with Terraform modules, an NGINX ingress controller, Prometheus and Grafana, and two secure pipelines, plus the Helm, cert-manager, ExternalDNS and Argo CD bonuses.","stages":[{"title":"The brief and the board","icon":"📋","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>This track walks you through the <strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://github.com/CoderCo-Learning/eks-assignment-v1\">CoderCo EKS assignment</a></strong>. The app is the <strong>2048 game</strong>: a static website (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) with no backend. Your job is to run it on <strong>Amazon EKS</strong> the way a platform team would.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  U([player]) --> R53[\"Route 53<br/>game.lab.example.com\"] --> NLB[NLB]\n  NLB --> IC[\"NGINX ingress controller<br/>TLS by cert-manager\"] --> SVC[Service] --> P[\"2048 pods<br/>private subnets\"]\n  GH[\"GitHub Actions<br/>Checkov · Trivy · ECR\"] --> P\n  TF[\"Terraform<br/>VPC · EKS · add-ons\"] --> NLB\n  PR[Prometheus] --> GF[Grafana]","caption":"What you'll build"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>Cost:</strong> EKS isn't free. The control plane is about $0.10/hour, plus two t3.large nodes, a NAT gateway and a load balancer. That's roughly <strong>$8–10 a day</strong> while it runs. Set an <strong>AWS Budget</strong> alert first, and run the clean-up stage at the end of <strong>every</strong> session.</p>\n</blockquote>"}],"steps":[{"title":"Read the marking criteria","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Criterion</th>\n<th>Points</th>\n<th>Stage</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Board / tickets</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Terraform for AWS infra (VPC + EKS, modules, IAM, SGs)</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>4–5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>NGINX Ingress Controller</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>7</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Monitoring: Prometheus + Grafana dashboard</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>9</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pipeline 1: Terraform</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pipeline 2: Trivy, Checkov, build → ECR, deploy</td>\n<td><strong>30</strong></td>\n<td>11</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonus: Argo CD</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>13</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonus: architecture diagram</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>14</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonus: Helm</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>12</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonus: cert-manager</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bonus: ExternalDNS</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td><strong>150</strong></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Which single area is worth the most points?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"The NGINX Ingress Controller","ok":false},{"t":"Monitoring","ok":false},{"t":"Pipeline 2: security scans, build and push to ECR, deploy to EKS","ok":true},{"t":"The board","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>30 points. The two pipelines together are worth 40, so plan your time around them.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Fork and clone the repo","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Fork <strong>CoderCo-Learning/eks-assignment-v1</strong> to your own GitHub account (call it <code>eks-assignment</code>), then clone it:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"git clone https://github.com/your-username/eks-assignment.git && cd eks-assignment","output":"Cloning into 'eks-assignment'...\nReceiving objects: 100% (42/42), 210.11 KiB | 4.12 MiB/s, done."},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Run the game locally to see what you're deploying:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"python3 -m http.server 3000","output":"Serving HTTP on 0.0.0.0 port 3000 (http://0.0.0.0:3000/) ..."},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Open <strong>http://localhost:3000</strong> and play a round.</p>"}]},{"title":"Set up the board","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Create a Trello or Jira board with columns <strong>To do → In progress → Review → Done</strong>. Each ticket should be small enough to finish in one session, with a clear \"done when\":</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Ticket</th>\n<th>Done when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Dockerfile</td>\n<td>the game is served on 8080 as non-root</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Bootstrap: S3 state + OIDC role</td>\n<td>bootstrap apply succeeds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>VPC module</td>\n<td>3 public + 3 private subnets, NAT, load balancer tags</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>EKS module + node group + access entries</td>\n<td><code>kubectl get nodes</code> shows 2 Ready</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>ECR repository</td>\n<td>immutable tags, scan on push</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>App manifests</td>\n<td>the game is reachable via port-forward</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>Delegate <code>lab</code> subdomain to Route 53</td>\n<td><code>dig NS</code> shows AWS servers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>NGINX Ingress Controller</td>\n<td>NLB created, IngressClass <code>nginx</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>cert-manager + ExternalDNS</td>\n<td>HTTPS padlock, record created automatically</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>Monitoring</td>\n<td>dashboards show nodes, pods, CPU and memory</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>11</td>\n<td>Pipeline 1</td>\n<td>the PR shows a plan; merge applies</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>Pipeline 2</td>\n<td>push deploys; a bad image fails the run</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>13</td>\n<td>Helm chart, Argo CD, diagram, README, clean-up script</td>\n<td>each committed and working</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 Move tickets as you go and link commits to them (e.g. <code>#7 delegate lab subdomain</code>). Marks are for tracking <strong>progress</strong>, not just having a board.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]}]},{"title":"Warm up on a local cluster","icon":"🧪","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Before paying for EKS, practise the same commands on a <strong>free</strong> cluster on your laptop with <strong>kind</strong> (Kubernetes in Docker).</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  L[\"💻 laptop\"] --> D[Docker] --> CP[\"kind control-plane\"] & W1[\"kind worker\"] & W2[\"kind worker\"]\n  K[kubectl] --> CP"}],"steps":[{"title":"Install the tools","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>On macOS: <code>brew install kind kubectl helm</code>. (Windows: <code>choco install kind kubernetes-cli kubernetes-helm</code>.)</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kind version && kubectl version --client && helm version --short","output":"kind v0.29.0 go1.24.2 darwin/arm64\nClient Version: v1.34.1\nv3.18.4+gd80839c"}]},{"title":"Create a three-node cluster","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"kind: Cluster\napiVersion: kind.x-k8s.io/v1alpha4\nnodes:\n  - role: control-plane\n  - role: worker\n  - role: worker","file":"kind-config.yaml"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kind create cluster --config kind-config.yaml --name k8s-demo","output":"Creating cluster \"k8s-demo\" ...\n ✓ Ensuring node image (kindest/node:v1.34.0) 🖼\n ✓ Preparing nodes 📦 📦 📦\n ✓ Starting control-plane 🕹️\n ✓ Joining worker nodes 🚜\nSet kubectl context to \"kind-k8s-demo\""},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl get nodes","output":"NAME                     STATUS   ROLES           AGE   VERSION\nk8s-demo-control-plane   Ready    control-plane   62s   v1.34.0\nk8s-demo-worker          Ready    <none>          41s   v1.34.0\nk8s-demo-worker2         Ready    <none>          41s   v1.34.0"}]},{"title":"Deploy, expose and self-heal","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl create deployment web --image=nginx:1.27 --replicas=3","output":"deployment.apps/web created"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl expose deployment web --port=80","output":"service/web exposed"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Now delete one pod and watch the Deployment replace it:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl delete pod -l app=web --wait=false && kubectl get pods -l app=web","output":"pod \"web-6d4cf56db6-2xkqp\" deleted\npod \"web-6d4cf56db6-9fz7m\" deleted\npod \"web-6d4cf56db6-qwl4c\" deleted\nNAME                   READY   STATUS              RESTARTS   AGE\nweb-6d4cf56db6-7hj2k   0/1     ContainerCreating   0          1s\nweb-6d4cf56db6-lm8vn   0/1     ContainerCreating   0          1s\nweb-6d4cf56db6-x4c9d   0/1     ContainerCreating   0          1s"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why did three new pods appear straight away?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"kubectl re-created them","ok":false},{"t":"The Deployment's ReplicaSet wants 3 replicas and keeps making reality match","ok":true},{"t":"kind restarts deleted containers","ok":false},{"t":"The Service recreated them","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Self-healing through desired state. To really remove them, delete the <strong>Deployment</strong>.</p>"}}]},{"title":"Reach it and tidy up","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl port-forward svc/web 8080:80","output":"Forwarding from 127.0.0.1:8080 -> 80\nHandling connection for 8080"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Visit http://localhost:8080, press Ctrl+C, then delete the practice cluster:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kind delete cluster --name k8s-demo","output":"Deleting cluster \"k8s-demo\" ...\nDeleted nodes: [\"k8s-demo-control-plane\" \"k8s-demo-worker\" \"k8s-demo-worker2\"]"}]}]},{"title":"Containerise 2048","icon":"🐳","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>2048 has no backend, so production needs only a <strong>web server for static files</strong>. Use the <strong>unprivileged nginx</strong> image: it already runs as a non-root user and listens on <strong>8080</strong> (non-root processes can't bind ports below 1024).</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  F[\"index.html · js/ · style/ · meta/\"] -->|COPY| I[\"nginx-unprivileged<br/>uid 101 · :8080\"] -->|push| ECR[(ECR game-2048:sha)]"}],"steps":[{"title":"The Dockerfile","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"dockerfile","code":"# Pin an exact version (or digest) from Docker Hub in real use\nFROM nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:stable-alpine\nCOPY --chown=101:101 index.html favicon.ico /usr/share/nginx/html/\nCOPY --chown=101:101 js/    /usr/share/nginx/html/js/\nCOPY --chown=101:101 style/ /usr/share/nginx/html/style/\nCOPY --chown=101:101 meta/  /usr/share/nginx/html/meta/\nEXPOSE 8080\n# no CMD needed: the base image starts nginx","file":"Dockerfile"},{"type":"code","lang":"gitignore","code":".git\n.github\nterraform/\nk8s/\ncharts/\n*.md\nRakefile","file":".dockerignore"},{"type":"html","html":"<p><code>--chown=101:101</code> gives the files to the nginx user. Copying only the site's folders keeps the build tooling and docs out of the image.</p>"}]},{"title":"Build for the right CPU","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>EKS t3 nodes are <strong>x86</strong>. On an Apple Silicon Mac, <code>--platform linux/amd64</code> stops \"exec format error\" later.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t game-2048:dev .","output":"[+] Building 6.3s (10/10) FINISHED\n => [1/5] FROM docker.io/nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:stable-alpine\n => [2/5] COPY --chown=101:101 index.html favicon.ico /usr/share/nginx/html/\n => naming to docker.io/library/game-2048:dev"}]},{"title":"Run it and prove it's not root","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"docker run -d -p 8080:8080 --name game game-2048:dev && curl -sI http://localhost:8080 | head -1","output":"a1b2c3d4e5f6…\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker exec game id","output":"uid=101(nginx) gid=101(nginx) groups=101(nginx)"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Which port must the Kubernetes Service's <code>targetPort</code> and the probes use for this image?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"80","ok":false},{"t":"3000","ok":false},{"t":"8080","ok":true},{"t":"443","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>The container listens on 8080. Port 3000 was only the local Python server.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Bootstrap: state and keyless CI","icon":"🪣","time":"30 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>As in the ECS track, two <strong>long-lived</strong> things come first, in their own small stack: an <strong>S3 bucket</strong> for Terraform state, and an <strong>OIDC role</strong> so GitHub Actions can reach AWS without stored keys.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  subgraph BOOT[\"terraform/bootstrap · applied once\"]\n    S3[(\"S3 state bucket<br/>versioned · encrypted\")]\n    OIDC[\"GitHub OIDC provider\"]\n    ROLE[\"github-actions role\"]\n  end\n  GHA[GitHub Actions] -->|AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity| ROLE"}],"steps":[{"title":"State bucket","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"state\" {\n  bucket = \"eks-lab-tfstate-example\"     # globally unique: use your own\n  lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }\n}\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_versioning\" \"state\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.state.id\n  versioning_configuration { status = \"Enabled\" }\n}\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block\" \"state\" {\n  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.state.id\n  block_public_acls       = true\n  block_public_policy     = true\n  ignore_public_acls      = true\n  restrict_public_buckets = true\n}","file":"terraform/bootstrap/state.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Add default encryption, and a bucket policy that denies non-HTTPS access.</p>"}]},{"title":"OIDC role, tied to your repo's main branch","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_iam_openid_connect_provider\" \"github\" {\n  url            = \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n  client_id_list = [\"sts.amazonaws.com\"]\n}\n\nresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"github_actions\" {\n  name = \"eks-lab-github-actions\"\n  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    Statement = [{\n      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n      Principal = { Federated = aws_iam_openid_connect_provider.github.arn }\n      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n      Condition = {\n        StringEquals = { \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\" }\n        StringLike   = { \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub\" = [\n          \"repo:your-username/eks-assignment:ref:refs/heads/main\",\n          \"repo:your-username/eks-assignment:pull_request\"\n        ] }\n      }\n    }]\n  })\n}","file":"terraform/bootstrap/oidc.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ Attaching broad permissions (even admin) is common for a first version. Note it in your README as something you'd scope down.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Apply it once","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"cd terraform/bootstrap && terraform init && terraform apply","output":"Plan: 6 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.\naws_s3_bucket.state: Creation complete after 2s [id=eks-lab-tfstate-example]\naws_iam_role.github_actions: Creation complete after 1s [id=eks-lab-github-actions]\nApply complete! Resources: 6 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Store the role's ARN as the GitHub secret <code>AWS_ROLE_ARN</code>.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why does the trust policy list <code>:pull_request</code> as well as <code>refs/heads/main</code>?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"So pull requests can apply changes to production","ok":false},{"t":"So Pipeline 1 can run <code>terraform plan</code> on pull requests; applies only happen from main","ok":true},{"t":"It's required by AWS","ok":false},{"t":"To allow forks to deploy","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>In production you'd give PRs a separate <strong>read-only</strong> plan role.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Terraform: VPC, EKS and ECR modules","icon":"🏗️","time":"90 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The criteria want <strong>reusable modules</strong>, with IAM and security groups configured properly. You'll wrap well-tested community modules in your own modules, then call them from an environment folder.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart TB\n  ENV[\"terraform/envs/dev<br/>main.tf · backend.tf · providers.tf · tfvars\"] --> VPC[\"modules/vpc\"]\n  ENV --> EKS[\"modules/eks\"]\n  ENV --> ECR[\"modules/ecr\"]\n  ENV --> IRSA[\"modules/irsa\"]\n  VPC -->|vpc_id, private_subnets| EKS\n  EKS -->|oidc_provider_arn| IRSA"}],"steps":[{"title":"Lay out the folders","blocks":[{"type":"output","text":"terraform/\n├── bootstrap/          # done: state bucket + OIDC role\n├── modules/\n│   ├── vpc/            # wraps terraform-aws-modules/vpc\n│   ├── eks/            # wraps terraform-aws-modules/eks + access entries\n│   ├── ecr/            # the image repository\n│   ├── irsa/           # one IAM role per add-on\n│   └── addons/         # helm_release: ingress, cert-manager, ExternalDNS, monitoring, Argo CD\n└── envs/\n    └── dev/            # calls the modules with dev values"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 Many teams split <strong>addons</strong> into a second stack applied after the cluster exists, because the Helm and Kubernetes providers need a live cluster to connect to.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"The VPC module","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"module \"vpc\" {\n  source  = \"terraform-aws-modules/vpc/aws\"\n  version = \"~> 6.0\"\n\n  name            = var.name\n  cidr            = var.cidr\n  azs             = var.azs\n  private_subnets = var.private_subnets\n  public_subnets  = var.public_subnets\n\n  enable_nat_gateway   = true\n  single_nat_gateway   = var.single_nat_gateway   # true for a lab: cheaper, but a single point of failure\n  enable_dns_hostnames = true\n\n  # tell AWS where to put load balancers created from Kubernetes\n  public_subnet_tags  = { \"kubernetes.io/role/elb\" = 1 }\n  private_subnet_tags = { \"kubernetes.io/role/internal-elb\" = 1 }\n}\n\noutput \"vpc_id\"          { value = module.vpc.vpc_id }\noutput \"private_subnets\" { value = module.vpc.private_subnets }","file":"terraform/modules/vpc/main.tf"}]},{"title":"The EKS module","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"module \"eks\" {\n  source  = \"terraform-aws-modules/eks/aws\"\n  version = \"~> 21.0\"\n\n  name               = var.name\n  kubernetes_version = var.kubernetes_version   # a version in standard support\n  vpc_id             = var.vpc_id\n  subnet_ids         = var.private_subnet_ids\n\n  endpoint_public_access                   = true   # lab only\n  enable_cluster_creator_admin_permissions = true\n  enable_irsa                              = true\n\n  eks_managed_node_groups = {\n    default = {\n      instance_types = [\"t3.large\"]\n      min_size       = 1\n      max_size       = 3\n      desired_size   = 2\n    }\n  }\n\n  access_entries = {\n    github_actions = {\n      principal_arn = var.github_actions_role_arn\n      policy_associations = {\n        admin = {\n          policy_arn   = \"arn:aws:eks::aws:cluster-access-policy/AmazonEKSClusterAdminPolicy\"\n          access_scope = { type = \"cluster\" }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}","file":"terraform/modules/eks/main.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ Without the <code>github_actions</code> access entry, Pipeline 2 fails later with \"You must be logged in to the server\".</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"ECR and the environment","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"aws_ecr_repository\" \"this\" {\n  name                 = var.name                 # game-2048\n  image_tag_mutability = \"IMMUTABLE\"\n  image_scanning_configuration { scan_on_push = true }\n}","file":"terraform/modules/ecr/main.tf"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"module \"vpc\" {\n  source          = \"../../modules/vpc\"\n  name            = \"eks-lab\"\n  cidr            = \"10.0.0.0/16\"\n  azs             = [\"eu-west-2a\", \"eu-west-2b\", \"eu-west-2c\"]\n  private_subnets = [\"10.0.1.0/24\", \"10.0.2.0/24\", \"10.0.3.0/24\"]\n  public_subnets  = [\"10.0.4.0/24\", \"10.0.5.0/24\", \"10.0.6.0/24\"]\n  single_nat_gateway = true\n}\n\nmodule \"eks\" {\n  source                 = \"../../modules/eks\"\n  name                   = \"eks-lab\"\n  kubernetes_version     = var.kubernetes_version\n  vpc_id                 = module.vpc.vpc_id\n  private_subnet_ids     = module.vpc.private_subnets\n  github_actions_role_arn = var.github_actions_role_arn\n}\n\nmodule \"ecr\" {\n  source = \"../../modules/ecr\"\n  name   = \"game-2048\"\n}","file":"terraform/envs/dev/main.tf"},{"type":"html","html":"<p><code>backend.tf</code> points at the bootstrap bucket with <code>use_lockfile = true</code>, exactly like the ECS track.</p>"}]},{"title":"Apply and connect kubectl","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"cd terraform/envs/dev && terraform init && terraform apply","output":"Plan: 63 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.\nmodule.eks.module.eks.aws_eks_cluster.this[0]: Still creating... [9m30s elapsed]\nmodule.eks.module.eks.aws_eks_cluster.this[0]: Creation complete after 9m48s [id=eks-lab]\nmodule.eks.module.eks.module.eks_managed_node_group[\"default\"].aws_eks_node_group.this[0]: Creation complete after 1m52s\nApply complete! Resources: 63 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed."},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws eks update-kubeconfig --region eu-west-2 --name eks-lab","output":"Added new context arn:aws:eks:eu-west-2:123456789012:cluster/eks-lab to /Users/you/.kube/config"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl get nodes","output":"NAME                                       STATUS   ROLES    AGE   VERSION\nip-10-0-1-87.eu-west-2.compute.internal    Ready    <none>   3m    v1.34.0-eks-…\nip-10-0-2-141.eu-west-2.compute.internal   Ready    <none>   3m    v1.34.0-eks-…"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The nodes' names start with <code>ip-10-0-1-…</code> and <code>ip-10-0-2-…</code>. What does that tell you?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"They're in public subnets","ok":false},{"t":"They're in the private subnets (10.0.1.0/24 and 10.0.2.0/24), spread across AZs","ok":true},{"t":"They have public IPs","ok":false},{"t":"They're Fargate nodes","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Nodes in private subnets, load balancers in public: the same pattern as the ECS track.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Deploy the game with manifests","icon":"🚢","time":"45 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Push an image to ECR, then deploy with plain Kubernetes YAML: a namespace, a Deployment and a ClusterIP Service.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  NS[namespace game] --> D[\"Deployment game<br/>2 replicas · probes · limits\"] --> P1[pod] & P2[pod]\n  S[\"Service game<br/>80 → 8080\"] --> P1 & P2"}],"steps":[{"title":"Push the first image","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"aws ecr get-login-password --region eu-west-2 | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com","output":"Login Succeeded"},{"type":"term","cmd":"docker tag game-2048:dev 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/game-2048:$(git rev-parse HEAD) && docker push 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/game-2048:$(git rev-parse HEAD)","output":"The push refers to repository [123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/game-2048]\n3f9c2e1…: digest: sha256:4b8e… size: 1989"}]},{"title":"The Deployment, hardened","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: game\n  namespace: game\nspec:\n  replicas: 2\n  selector:\n    matchLabels: { app: game }\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels: { app: game }\n    spec:\n      containers:\n        - name: game\n          image: IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER          # the pipeline swaps in …/game-2048:<sha>\n          ports:\n            - containerPort: 8080\n          resources:\n            requests: { cpu: 50m, memory: 64Mi }\n            limits: { memory: 128Mi }\n          readinessProbe:\n            httpGet: { path: /, port: 8080 }\n            initialDelaySeconds: 3\n            periodSeconds: 5\n          livenessProbe:\n            httpGet: { path: /, port: 8080 }\n            initialDelaySeconds: 10\n            periodSeconds: 10\n          securityContext:\n            runAsNonRoot: true\n            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n            capabilities: { drop: [\"ALL\"] }\n          volumeMounts:\n            - { name: tmp, mountPath: /tmp }   # nginx needs a writable /tmp\n      volumes:\n        - { name: tmp, emptyDir: {} }","file":"k8s/deployment.yaml"}]},{"title":"Namespace and Service","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"apiVersion: v1\nkind: Namespace\nmetadata:\n  name: game","file":"k8s/namespace.yaml"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"apiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata:\n  name: game\n  namespace: game\nspec:\n  selector: { app: game }\n  ports:\n    - port: 80\n      targetPort: 8080","file":"k8s/service.yaml"}]},{"title":"Apply and watch the rollout","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Swap the placeholder for your image locally (the pipeline will do this later), then apply:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl apply -f k8s/namespace.yaml && kubectl apply -f k8s/","output":"namespace/game created\ndeployment.apps/game created\nservice/game created"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl rollout status deployment/game -n game","output":"Waiting for deployment \"game\" rollout to finish: 0 of 2 updated replicas are available...\nWaiting for deployment \"game\" rollout to finish: 1 of 2 updated replicas are available...\ndeployment \"game\" successfully rolled out"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl port-forward -n game svc/game 8080:80","output":"Forwarding from 127.0.0.1:8080 -> 8080"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why is the container given an <code>emptyDir</code> mounted at <code>/tmp</code>?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"To store the game's high scores permanently","ok":false},{"t":"<code>readOnlyRootFilesystem: true</code> makes the image read-only, but nginx needs to write temp files, so a scratch <code>emptyDir</code> gives it somewhere writable","ok":true},{"t":"To share files with the Service","ok":false},{"t":"emptyDir is required by EKS","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Hardening (read-only root) plus a small writable scratch space is a common pattern.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"DNS and the NGINX Ingress Controller","icon":"🌐","time":"60 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Now let the internet in through <strong>one</strong> load balancer and an <strong>NGINX ingress controller</strong>.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  U([browser]) --> R53[\"Route 53 zone<br/>lab.example.com\"] --> NLB[\"NLB (from the controller's<br/>LoadBalancer Service)\"]\n  NLB --> IC[\"NGINX Ingress Controller<br/>IngressClass nginx\"] -->|\"host: game.lab…\"| S[Service game] --> P[pods]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Delegate a subdomain to Route 53","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Keep the domain at its registrar and hand <strong><code>lab.example.com</code></strong> to AWS:\n1. Route 53 → <strong>Create hosted zone</strong> <code>lab.example.com</code> (public). Note its 4 NS servers.\n2. At the registrar, add 4 <strong>NS</strong> records named <code>lab</code>, one per AWS server.</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"dig NS lab.example.com +short","output":"ns-1234.awsdns-26.org.\nns-567.awsdns-06.net.\nns-89.awsdns-11.com.\nns-1890.awsdns-44.co.uk."}]},{"title":"Choose the controller","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The community <strong>ingress-nginx</strong> project has been <strong>retired</strong>: it no longer gets releases or security fixes. Install <strong>F5's maintained NGINX Ingress Controller</strong> instead. It's still an NGINX Ingress Controller, so it meets the criterion, and explaining <strong>why</strong> you chose it in your README shows you keep up to date.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Community ingress-nginx</th>\n<th>F5 NGINX Ingress Controller</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Status</td>\n<td>retired</td>\n<td>maintained</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Annotations</td>\n<td><code>nginx.ingress.kubernetes.io/…</code></td>\n<td><code>nginx.org/…</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"}]},{"title":"Install it with Terraform","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"helm_release\" \"nginx_ingress\" {\n  name             = \"nginx-ingress\"\n  repository       = \"oci://ghcr.io/nginx/charts\"\n  chart            = \"nginx-ingress\"\n  # version        = \"…\"   ← pin the chart version you tested\n  namespace        = \"nginx-ingress\"\n  create_namespace = true\n\n  values = [yamlencode({\n    controller = {\n      ingressClass = { name = \"nginx\", setAsDefaultIngress = true }\n      service = {\n        type = \"LoadBalancer\"\n        annotations = { \"service.beta.kubernetes.io/aws-load-balancer-type\" = \"nlb\" }\n      }\n    }\n  })]\n}","file":"terraform/modules/addons/ingress.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl get svc -n nginx-ingress","output":"NAME                       TYPE           EXTERNAL-IP                                                 PORT(S)\nnginx-ingress-controller   LoadBalancer   a1b2c3…elb.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com                         80:31080/TCP,443:31443/TCP"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl get ingressclass","output":"NAME    CONTROLLER                     AGE\nnginx   nginx.org/ingress-controller   4m"}]},{"title":"An Ingress for the game","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Ingress\nmetadata:\n  name: game\n  namespace: game\nspec:\n  ingressClassName: nginx\n  rules:\n    - host: game.lab.example.com\n      http:\n        paths:\n          - path: /\n            pathType: Prefix\n            backend:\n              service:\n                name: game\n                port: { number: 80 }","file":"k8s/ingress.yaml"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Before DNS exists, test by sending the Host header straight to the NLB:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"curl -sI -H \"Host: game.lab.example.com\" http://a1b2c3…elb.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com | head -1","output":"HTTP/1.1 200 OK"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The controller's Service shows <code>EXTERNAL-IP &lt;pending&gt;</code> for a long time. What do you check?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"The Grafana password","ok":false},{"t":"<code>kubectl describe svc -n nginx-ingress</code> events, and that the public subnets carry <code>kubernetes.io/role/elb = 1</code>","ok":true},{"t":"The ECR repository","ok":false},{"t":"The Ingress hostname","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>AWS needs those tags to choose subnets for the load balancer.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"HTTPS and DNS on autopilot (bonus)","icon":"🔐","time":"60 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p><strong>cert-manager</strong> gets free Let's Encrypt certificates and renews them. <strong>ExternalDNS</strong> creates Route 53 records from your Ingresses. Both need AWS permissions, through <strong>IRSA</strong>.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"sequenceDiagram\n  participant ING as Ingress game\n  participant ED as ExternalDNS\n  participant CM as cert-manager\n  participant R53 as Route 53\n  participant LE as Let's Encrypt\n  ING->>ED: host game.lab.example.com\n  ED->>R53: A/ALIAS → NLB (+ TXT owner record)\n  ING->>CM: tls + cluster-issuer annotation\n  CM->>R53: TXT _acme-challenge (DNS-01)\n  LE->>R53: verify\n  LE-->>CM: certificate → Secret game-tls"}],"steps":[{"title":"IAM roles for the two add-ons","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>One IRSA role each, limited to <strong>one hosted zone</strong> and <strong>one service account</strong>:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"module \"cert_manager_irsa\" {\n  source  = \"terraform-aws-modules/iam/aws//modules/iam-role-for-service-accounts-eks\"\n  version = \"~> 5.0\"   # newer major versions renamed this submodule: check its docs\n\n  role_name                     = \"eks-lab-cert-manager\"\n  attach_cert_manager_policy    = true\n  cert_manager_hosted_zone_arns = [var.hosted_zone_arn]\n  oidc_providers = {\n    main = {\n      provider_arn               = var.oidc_provider_arn\n      namespace_service_accounts = [\"cert-manager:cert-manager\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nmodule \"external_dns_irsa\" {\n  source  = \"terraform-aws-modules/iam/aws//modules/iam-role-for-service-accounts-eks\"\n  version = \"~> 5.0\"\n\n  role_name                     = \"eks-lab-external-dns\"\n  attach_external_dns_policy    = true\n  external_dns_hosted_zone_arns = [var.hosted_zone_arn]\n  oidc_providers = {\n    main = {\n      provider_arn               = var.oidc_provider_arn\n      namespace_service_accounts = [\"external-dns:external-dns\"]\n    }\n  }\n}","file":"terraform/modules/irsa/main.tf"}]},{"title":"Install cert-manager and ExternalDNS","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"helm_release\" \"cert_manager\" {\n  name             = \"cert-manager\"\n  repository       = \"https://charts.jetstack.io\"\n  chart            = \"cert-manager\"\n  namespace        = \"cert-manager\"\n  create_namespace = true\n  set = [\n    { name = \"crds.enabled\", value = \"true\" },\n    { name = \"serviceAccount.annotations.eks\\\\.amazonaws\\\\.com/role-arn\", value = var.cert_manager_role_arn },\n  ]\n}\n\nresource \"helm_release\" \"external_dns\" {\n  name             = \"external-dns\"\n  repository       = \"https://kubernetes-sigs.github.io/external-dns/\"\n  chart            = \"external-dns\"\n  namespace        = \"external-dns\"\n  create_namespace = true\n  values = [yamlencode({\n    provider      = { name = \"aws\" }\n    domainFilters = [\"lab.example.com\"]\n    policy        = \"sync\"\n    txtOwnerId    = \"eks-lab\"\n    serviceAccount = { annotations = { \"eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn\" = var.external_dns_role_arn } }\n  })]\n}","file":"terraform/modules/addons/dns-tls.tf"}]},{"title":"A ClusterIssuer (staging first)","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"apiVersion: cert-manager.io/v1\nkind: ClusterIssuer\nmetadata:\n  name: letsencrypt\nspec:\n  acme:\n    server: https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory\n    email: you@example.com\n    privateKeySecretRef: { name: letsencrypt }\n    solvers:\n      - dns01:\n          route53: { region: eu-west-2 }\n        selector:\n          dnsZones: [lab.example.com]","file":"k8s/cluster-issuer.yaml"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ Use <strong>staging</strong> until the whole flow works (production has rate limits), then change <code>server</code> to <code>https://acme-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Turn on HTTPS for the game","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Add the annotation and a <code>tls</code> block to <code>k8s/ingress.yaml</code>:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"metadata:\n  annotations:\n    cert-manager.io/cluster-issuer: letsencrypt\nspec:\n  tls:\n    - hosts: [game.lab.example.com]\n      secretName: game-tls","file":"k8s/ingress.yaml"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl get certificate -n game","output":"NAME       READY   SECRET     AGE\ngame-tls   True    game-tls   2m"},{"type":"term","cmd":"dig +short game.lab.example.com","output":"a1b2c3…elb.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com.\n18.170.42.11\n35.177.8.200"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Open <strong>https://game.lab.example.com</strong>. The padlock and DNS record arrived with no manual steps.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>A certificate stays <code>READY False</code>. Where do you start?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Restart the nodes","ok":false},{"t":"<code>kubectl describe certificate</code>, then follow its CertificateRequest → Order → Challenge, and check the cert-manager logs (often the IRSA role can't write the TXT record)","ok":true},{"t":"Delete the Route 53 zone","ok":false},{"t":"Switch the Service to NodePort","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>cert-manager leaves a trail of objects. Follow them until you find the error.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Monitoring with Prometheus and Grafana","icon":"📈","time":"60 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Worth <strong>15 points</strong>: Prometheus and Grafana, with a dashboard showing CPU, memory, pods, nodes and namespaces.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  NE[node-exporter] --> P[(Prometheus)]\n  KSM[kube-state-metrics] --> P\n  KL[kubelet / cAdvisor] --> P\n  P --> G[\"Grafana<br/>grafana.lab.example.com\"]\n  P --> AM[Alertmanager]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Install kube-prometheus-stack","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"helm_release\" \"monitoring\" {\n  name             = \"monitoring\"\n  repository       = \"https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts\"\n  chart            = \"kube-prometheus-stack\"\n  # version        = \"…\"   ← pin what you tested\n  namespace        = \"monitoring\"\n  create_namespace = true\n  values           = [file(\"${path.module}/values/monitoring.yaml\")]\n}","file":"terraform/modules/addons/monitoring.tf"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"grafana:\n  ingress:\n    enabled: true\n    ingressClassName: nginx\n    annotations:\n      cert-manager.io/cluster-issuer: letsencrypt\n    hosts: [grafana.lab.example.com]\n    tls:\n      - hosts: [grafana.lab.example.com]\n        secretName: grafana-tls\nprometheus:\n  prometheusSpec:\n    retention: 7d","file":"terraform/modules/addons/values/monitoring.yaml"}]},{"title":"Log in to Grafana","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl get pods -n monitoring","output":"NAME                                                     READY   STATUS    AGE\nalertmanager-monitoring-kube-prometheus-alertmanager-0   2/2     Running   3m\nmonitoring-grafana-6d8f9c7b5-x2k4p                       3/3     Running   3m\nmonitoring-kube-state-metrics-7b9f6d4c8-q8r2t            1/1     Running   3m\nmonitoring-prometheus-node-exporter-4lq9v                1/1     Running   3m\nprometheus-monitoring-kube-prometheus-prometheus-0       2/2     Running   3m"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl get secret -n monitoring monitoring-grafana -o jsonpath=\"{.data.admin-password}\" | base64 -d","output":"pr0m-0p3r4t0r"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Log in as <code>admin</code> at https://grafana.lab.example.com, then change the password (or set <code>grafana.adminPassword</code> from a secret).</p>"}]},{"title":"Build your own dashboard","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The built-in <strong>Kubernetes / Compute Resources / Cluster</strong> and <strong>Node Exporter / Nodes</strong> dashboards cover the basics. For extra marks, build one with four panels:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Panel</th>\n<th>PromQL</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Running pods per namespace</td>\n<td><code>sum by (namespace) (kube_pod_status_phase{phase=\"Running\"})</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Node count</td>\n<td><code>count(kube_node_info)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CPU by namespace</td>\n<td><code>sum by (namespace) (rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{container!=\"\"}[5m]))</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Memory by namespace</td>\n<td><code>sum by (namespace) (container_memory_working_set_bytes{container!=\"\"})</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Export it (Dashboard → Share → Export → JSON) into <code>monitoring/dashboards/</code> in your repo.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why do the requests and limits you set on the game make these graphs more useful?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Prometheus can't scrape pods without them","ok":false},{"t":"You can compare actual usage against what each pod reserved and is allowed, which shows over- or under-sizing","ok":true},{"t":"Grafana requires limits to start","ok":false},{"t":"They change the colours","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Usage on its own is just a number. Against requests and limits, it becomes a decision.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Pipeline 1: Terraform","icon":"🔁","time":"45 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Automate the infrastructure: <strong>plan on every pull request</strong>, <strong>apply on merge</strong>, with state management and error handling.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  PR[pull request] --> F[\"fmt -check · validate\"] --> PL[\"plan -detailed-exitcode\"]\n  PL -->|exit 1| X[❌ fail]\n  PL -->|exit 2 on main| AP[\"apply tfplan\"]\n  PL -->|exit 0| OK[\"✅ no changes\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"The workflow","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"name: Terraform\non:\n  pull_request:\n    paths: ['terraform/**']\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n    paths: ['terraform/**']\n  workflow_dispatch:\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: terraform-dev\n  cancel-in-progress: false      # never kill an apply half-way\n\npermissions:\n  id-token: write\n  contents: read\n  pull-requests: write\n\njobs:\n  terraform:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    environment: dev             # add required reviewers here for an approval gate\n    defaults:\n      run:\n        working-directory: terraform/envs/dev\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: ${{ secrets.AWS_ROLE_ARN }}\n          aws-region: eu-west-2\n      - uses: hashicorp/setup-terraform@v3\n      - run: terraform fmt -check -recursive\n      - run: terraform init -input=false\n      - run: terraform validate\n      - id: plan\n        run: terraform plan -input=false -out=tfplan -detailed-exitcode\n        continue-on-error: true\n      - if: steps.plan.outputs.exitcode == '1'\n        run: exit 1\n      - if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' && steps.plan.outputs.exitcode == '2'\n        run: terraform apply -input=false tfplan","file":".github/workflows/terraform.yml"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>🔧 Pin third-party actions to full commit SHAs in real use, and check for newer major versions.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"What \"state management and error handling\" mean","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<ul>\n<li><strong>State:</strong> remote in S3, versioned, <code>use_lockfile = true</code>, created by bootstrap, plus a <strong>concurrency group</strong> so two runs can't fight over the lock.</li>\n<li><strong>Errors:</strong> <code>fmt -check</code> and <code>validate</code> fail fast. <code>-detailed-exitcode</code> separates <strong>error (1)</strong> from <strong>changes (2)</strong> and <strong>no changes (0)</strong>. <code>-input=false</code> never hangs. Only the <strong>saved plan</strong> is applied, and only on <strong>main</strong>.</li>\n</ul>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why <code>continue-on-error: true</code> on the plan step?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"To ignore Terraform errors","ok":false},{"t":"Exit code 2 means \"there are changes\", which isn't a failure; the next step fails the job explicitly when the code is 1","ok":true},{"t":"To speed up the run","ok":false},{"t":"It's required by setup-terraform","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>The workflow decides what each exit code means, rather than treating every non-zero code as a failure.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Pipeline 2: scan, build, push and deploy","icon":"🛡️","time":"60 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>The biggest section (<strong>30 points</strong>): <strong>Checkov</strong> scans the code, <strong>Trivy</strong> scans the image <strong>before</strong> it's pushed, the image goes to <strong>ECR</strong> tagged with the commit SHA, and the manifests deploy to EKS with <strong>automatic rollback</strong>.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  A[Checkov] --> B[docker build] --> C[Trivy] --> D[\"push to ECR<br/>:sha\"] --> E[\"kubectl apply\"] --> F{\"rollout status\"}\n  F -->|timeout| G[\"rollout undo · exit 1\"]\n  F -->|ready| H[✅]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Scan, then build","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"name: App\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n    paths: ['index.html', 'js/**', 'style/**', 'meta/**', 'k8s/**', 'Dockerfile']\n  workflow_dispatch:\npermissions:\n  id-token: write\n  contents: read\nenv:\n  AWS_REGION: eu-west-2\n  ECR_REPOSITORY: game-2048\n  IMAGE_TAG: ${{ github.sha }}\njobs:\n  scan-build-deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n      - name: Checkov (Kubernetes YAML + Dockerfile)\n        uses: bridgecrewio/checkov-action@v12\n        with:\n          directory: .\n          framework: kubernetes,dockerfile\n          soft_fail: false\n      - name: Build\n        run: docker build -t \"$ECR_REPOSITORY:$IMAGE_TAG\" .","file":".github/workflows/app.yml"}]},{"title":"Trivy, then push","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"      - name: Trivy (fail on fixable HIGH/CRITICAL)\n        uses: aquasecurity/trivy-action@0.28.0     # pin to a full commit SHA in real use\n        with:\n          image-ref: ${{ env.ECR_REPOSITORY }}:${{ env.IMAGE_TAG }}\n          severity: CRITICAL,HIGH\n          ignore-unfixed: true\n          exit-code: '1'\n      - uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4\n        with:\n          role-to-assume: ${{ secrets.AWS_ROLE_ARN }}\n          aws-region: ${{ env.AWS_REGION }}\n      - id: ecr\n        uses: aws-actions/amazon-ecr-login@v2\n      - name: Push\n        run: |\n          IMAGE=\"${{ steps.ecr.outputs.registry }}/$ECR_REPOSITORY:$IMAGE_TAG\"\n          docker tag \"$ECR_REPOSITORY:$IMAGE_TAG\" \"$IMAGE\"\n          docker push \"$IMAGE\"\n          echo \"IMAGE=$IMAGE\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"","file":".github/workflows/app.yml"}]},{"title":"Deploy with automatic rollback","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"      - name: Deploy\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          aws eks update-kubeconfig --region \"$AWS_REGION\" --name eks-lab\n          sed -i \"s#IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER#${IMAGE}#\" k8s/deployment.yaml\n          kubectl apply -f k8s/namespace.yaml\n          kubectl apply -f k8s/\n          if ! kubectl rollout status deployment/game -n game --timeout=120s; then\n            echo \"Rollout failed: rolling back\"\n            kubectl rollout undo deployment/game -n game\n            exit 1\n          fi","file":".github/workflows/app.yml"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why this order: Checkov is cheap and catches design flaws early. A vulnerable image <strong>never reaches ECR</strong>. OIDC means no stored keys. SHA tags make rollbacks exact. <code>rollout status</code> + <code>undo</code> turns a bad release into a red run, with the old version still serving.</p>"}]},{"title":"Fix what the scanners find","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Typical Checkov findings on Kubernetes YAML: no <strong>requests/limits</strong>, no <strong>probes</strong>, running as <strong>root</strong>, an image tag of <strong><code>latest</code></strong>, no <strong>securityContext</strong>. The hardened Deployment from stage 6 already fixes most of them.</p>\n<p>To accept a finding deliberately, add a reasoned skip:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"metadata:\n  annotations:\n    checkov.io/skip1: CKV_K8S_43=Image is pinned by commit SHA tag, not digest"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Trivy findings are usually fixed by a <strong>newer base image</strong>: pin a newer version and rebuild.</p>"}]},{"title":"Prove the error handling works","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Break the readiness probe on purpose (e.g. path <code>/nope</code>), push it, and watch the run:</p>"},{"type":"term","cmd":"gh run watch","output":"✓ Checkov (Kubernetes YAML + Dockerfile)\n✓ Build\n✓ Trivy (fail on fixable HIGH/CRITICAL)\n✓ Push\nX Deploy\n  Waiting for deployment \"game\" rollout to finish: 1 out of 2 new replicas have been updated...\n  error: timed out waiting for the condition\n  Rollout failed: rolling back\n  deployment.apps/game rolled back"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>During that failed rollout, were players affected?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Yes: all pods were replaced with the broken version","ok":false},{"t":"No: the new pods never became ready, so the Service kept sending traffic to the old pods, and the pipeline rolled back","ok":true},{"t":"Yes: the namespace was deleted","ok":false},{"t":"Only for 120 seconds","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Readiness probes gate the rollout. That's why they matter so much.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Helm chart for the app (bonus)","icon":"⎈","time":"45 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Turn the three manifests into a <strong>Helm chart</strong>, so each release only changes a value: the image tag.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  T[\"templates/<br/>deployment · service · ingress\"] --> H{helm}\n  V[\"values.yaml<br/>image.tag · host · replicas\"] --> H\n  H --> K[EKS]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Create and trim the chart","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"helm create charts/game-2048","output":"Creating charts/game-2048"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Delete the generated templates you don't need, and move your three manifests into <code>templates/</code>, replacing fixed values with <code>{{ .Values… }}</code>.</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"replicaCount: 2\nimage:\n  repository: 123456789012.dkr.ecr.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/game-2048\n  tag: \"\"                       # set by the pipeline\ningress:\n  host: game.lab.example.com\n  clusterIssuer: letsencrypt","file":"charts/game-2048/values.yaml"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"spec:\n  replicas: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}\n  template:\n    spec:\n      containers:\n        - name: game\n          image: \"{{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ required \"image.tag is required\" .Values.image.tag }}\"","file":"charts/game-2048/templates/deployment.yaml"}]},{"title":"Lint, render and install","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"helm lint charts/game-2048 --set image.tag=test","output":"==> Linting charts/game-2048\n1 chart(s) linted, 0 chart(s) failed"},{"type":"term","cmd":"helm upgrade --install game charts/game-2048 -n game --create-namespace --set image.tag=3f9c2e1","output":"Release \"game\" does not exist. Installing it now.\nNAME: game\nNAMESPACE: game\nSTATUS: deployed\nREVISION: 1"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>In Pipeline 2, replace the <code>sed</code> + <code>kubectl apply</code> lines with <code>helm upgrade --install … --set image.tag=$IMAGE_TAG --wait --atomic</code>. <code>--atomic</code> rolls back automatically if the release doesn't become healthy.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What does <code>--atomic</code> add to <code>helm upgrade --install</code>?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"It makes the upgrade faster","ok":false},{"t":"If the release fails (e.g. pods never become ready within <code>--wait</code>), Helm rolls it back automatically","ok":true},{"t":"It deletes the namespace on failure","ok":false},{"t":"It skips the hooks","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>The Helm equivalent of <code>rollout status</code> + <code>rollout undo</code>.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"GitOps with Argo CD (bonus)","icon":"🐙","time":"60 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>With <strong>Argo CD</strong>, the pipeline stops deploying. It <strong>commits the new image tag to Git</strong>, and Argo CD (inside the cluster) syncs the cluster to match.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  CI[\"Pipeline 2<br/>scan · build · push\"] -->|\"commit image.tag=sha\"| REPO[(Git repo)]\n  ARGO[\"Argo CD<br/>in the cluster\"] -->|watches| REPO\n  ARGO -->|sync · prune · self-heal| K[EKS]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Install Argo CD","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"hcl","code":"resource \"helm_release\" \"argocd\" {\n  name             = \"argo-cd\"\n  repository       = \"https://argoproj.github.io/argo-helm\"\n  chart            = \"argo-cd\"\n  namespace        = \"argocd\"\n  create_namespace = true\n  values = [yamlencode({\n    configs = { params = { \"server.insecure\" = true } }   # TLS ends at the ingress\n    server = {\n      ingress = {\n        enabled          = true\n        ingressClassName = \"nginx\"\n        hostname         = \"argocd.lab.example.com\"\n        annotations      = { \"cert-manager.io/cluster-issuer\" = \"letsencrypt\" }\n        tls              = true\n      }\n    }\n  })]\n}","file":"terraform/modules/addons/argocd.tf"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath=\"{.data.password}\" | base64 -d","output":"xK3pR9vT2mQw7LbN"}]},{"title":"Point Argo CD at the chart","blocks":[{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1\nkind: Application\nmetadata:\n  name: game\n  namespace: argocd\nspec:\n  project: default\n  source:\n    repoURL: https://github.com/your-username/eks-assignment\n    targetRevision: main\n    path: charts/game-2048\n    helm:\n      valueFiles: [values.yaml]\n  destination:\n    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc\n    namespace: game\n  syncPolicy:\n    automated: { prune: true, selfHeal: true }\n    syncOptions: [CreateNamespace=true]","file":"argocd/game.yaml"},{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl apply -f argocd/game.yaml","output":"application.argoproj.io/game created"}]},{"title":"Change Pipeline 2's last step","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Instead of deploying, the pipeline commits the new tag:</p>"},{"type":"code","lang":"yaml","code":"      - name: Bump image tag for Argo CD\n        run: |\n          yq -i \".image.tag = \\\"$IMAGE_TAG\\\"\" charts/game-2048/values.yaml\n          git config user.name \"github-actions\"\n          git config user.email \"github-actions@users.noreply.github.com\"\n          git commit -am \"deploy: game-2048 $IMAGE_TAG [skip ci]\"\n          git push","file":".github/workflows/app.yml"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>The job now needs <code>contents: write</code>, and <strong>no</strong> cluster access at all.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>What's the security benefit of the GitOps version?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Argo CD encrypts the images","ok":false},{"t":"The pipeline no longer needs credentials for the cluster; only Argo CD, inside the cluster, applies changes","ok":true},{"t":"GitHub can't be hacked","ok":false},{"t":"It removes the need for Trivy","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Fewer powerful credentials outside the cluster means a smaller blast radius.</p>"}}]}]},{"title":"Architecture diagram and README (bonus)","icon":"📐","time":"45 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Worth 10 bonus points, and it's what reviewers read first. Draw it in <strong>draw.io</strong> or <strong>Excalidraw</strong> with AWS icons, and show <strong>two views</strong>.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  U([player]) --> R53[Route 53] --> NLB[NLB] --> IC[\"NGINX Ingress<br/>(cert-manager TLS)\"] --> S[Service] --> P[\"game pods<br/>private subnets\"]\n  ED[ExternalDNS] -.records.-> R53","caption":"View 1: the request flow"}],"steps":[{"title":"View 2: the deployment flow","blocks":[{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  DEV[developer] --> GH[GitHub]\n  GH --> P1[\"Pipeline 1<br/>Terraform plan/apply\"] --> AWS[\"VPC · EKS · IAM<br/>(state in S3)\"]\n  GH --> P2[\"Pipeline 2<br/>Checkov → build → Trivy → ECR\"] --> ARGO[\"Argo CD / kubectl\"] --> EKS[EKS]"}]},{"title":"The README checklist","blocks":[{"type":"html","html":"<ul>\n<li>what it is, and a screenshot of the live game</li>\n<li><strong>both diagrams</strong></li>\n<li>tools and <strong>why</strong> (e.g. \"F5 NGINX Ingress Controller, because community ingress-nginx is retired\")</li>\n<li>how to deploy, and how to <strong>destroy</strong></li>\n<li><strong>costs</strong>, and how you kept them down</li>\n<li>what you'd improve (least-privilege CI role, private API endpoint, NAT per AZ, Pod Identity, Gateway API)</li>\n<li>clear, ticket-linked commit messages from day one</li>\n</ul>"}]}]},{"title":"Clean up (do this, or pay for it)","icon":"🧹","time":"20 min","intro":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Kubernetes created some AWS resources itself: the <strong>NLB</strong>, the <strong>DNS records</strong> and any <strong>EBS volumes</strong>. Terraform doesn't know about them. Destroy the cluster first and they become <strong>orphans</strong> that keep billing and can block the VPC from being deleted. Tidy up <strong>inside out</strong>.</p>"},{"type":"diagram","code":"flowchart LR\n  A[\"1. Argo CD apps\"] --> B[\"2. Helm releases<br/>(NLB goes)\"] --> C[\"3. terraform destroy\"] --> D[\"4. check the console\"]"}],"steps":[{"title":"Remove the apps and add-ons","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"kubectl delete application game -n argocd","output":"application.argoproj.io \"game\" deleted"},{"type":"term","cmd":"helm uninstall argo-cd -n argocd && helm uninstall monitoring -n monitoring && helm uninstall external-dns -n external-dns && helm uninstall cert-manager -n cert-manager && helm uninstall nginx-ingress -n nginx-ingress","output":"release \"argo-cd\" uninstalled\nrelease \"monitoring\" uninstalled\nrelease \"external-dns\" uninstalled\nrelease \"cert-manager\" uninstalled\nrelease \"nginx-ingress\" uninstalled"},{"type":"html","html":"<blockquote>\n<p>If the add-ons are managed by Terraform, destroy the <strong>addons</strong> stack first instead of using <code>helm uninstall</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>"}]},{"title":"Destroy the infrastructure","blocks":[{"type":"term","cmd":"cd terraform/envs/dev && terraform destroy","output":"Plan: 0 to add, 0 to change, 63 to destroy.\nmodule.eks.module.eks.aws_eks_cluster.this[0]: Destruction complete after 6m12s\nmodule.vpc.module.vpc.aws_vpc.this[0]: Destruction complete after 1s\nDestroy complete! Resources: 63 destroyed."},{"type":"term","cmd":"aws elbv2 describe-load-balancers --region eu-west-2 --query \"LoadBalancers[].LoadBalancerName\"","output":"[]"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>Also check Route 53 records and EC2 → Volumes. Keep the bootstrap stack (state bucket and OIDC) for next time.</p>"},{"type":"check","mcq":{"q":[{"type":"html","html":"<p>Why delete the Helm releases <strong>before</strong> <code>terraform destroy</code>?</p>"}],"options":[{"t":"Helm releases cost more than the cluster","ok":false},{"t":"Removing the controller's LoadBalancer Service deletes the NLB that Kubernetes created; otherwise it's orphaned and blocks the VPC deletion","ok":true},{"t":"Terraform can't delete namespaces","ok":false},{"t":"Helm locks the state file","ok":false}],"explain":"<p>Inside-out clean-up: what Kubernetes created, Kubernetes should delete.</p>"}}]}]}]}];
